      "claim": "The modern definition of 'fair trade' requires voluntary exchange between independent parties with roughly equal bargaining power and equitable terms.",
      "evidence": "Standard definitions from Fairtrade International and economic ethics literature emphasize consent, equity, and the absence of coercion as core criteria.",
      "weight": 0.15,
